. But the user\'s application is in a specific namespace. This is a bit confusing. However, the user\'s first step was to use get_services, so maybe I should proceed with that. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the get_services tool is part of the monitoring stack and returns services that are being monitored. But without more info, I have to follow the user\'s initial choice. So the correct tool call is get_services with no arguments. \n\nSo the tool call would be:\n\n{"name": "get_services", "arguments": {}}\n\nThat\'s the correct step here. Once I have the list of services, I can then check each one\'s metrics, dependencies, and logs. But for now, the first step is to get the services.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{}', 'name': 'get_services'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-ae2914dbbb0953d3', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 852, 'prompt_tokens': 2473, 'total_tokens': 3325, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbd9-86dc-7b11-a8bb-d379aec90c50-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'get_services', 'args': {}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-ae2914dbbb0953d3', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2473, 'output_tokens': 852, 'total_tokens': 3325}), ToolMessage(content='meta=None content=[TextContent(type=\'text\', text="[\'cart\', \'flagd\', \'frontend-proxy\']", annotations=None)] isError=False', id='4e1e2dac-c6cd-42ba-830e-0d3fc5efa964', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-ae2914dbbb0953d3'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='8fe49029-8070-4321-9d67-73f95dcabc89')]]
