 the root cause and submitted the answer, the next step is to ensure that the answer is correctly formatted and submitted. The final answer should clearly state the root cause, which is the missing readiness probe in product-catalog, leading to connection issues and readiness failures.\n</think>\n\nsubmit_tool  \n{"ans": "The root cause of the frontend readiness issues is the absence of a readiness probe in the `product-catalog` deployment. This causes Kubernetes to incorrectly mark the pod as \'Ready\' without verifying the application is operational, leading to connection failures and timeouts. The `ad` and `cart` services may also have similar misconfigurations, but `product-catalog` is the most direct culprit."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=520, prompt_tokens=16162, total_tokens=16682, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbdc-cdf8-7923-83c3-f149e721b2bc-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 16162, 'output_tokens': 520, 'total_tokens': 16682}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='4c27a7b6-7e19-4665-a03c-7dd4ea1c353f')]]
