ht need to check both. However, since the user can only choose one tool call, they need to pick the most relevant one. \n\nAlternatively, using get_metrics to check for errors or latency. \n\nBut without knowing the exact metric names, it\'s challenging. \n\nAlternatively, the user could check the logs of the services using kubectl logs, but that requires knowing the pod names. \n\nBut the user hasn\'t done that yet. \n\nGiven the available tools, the next step could be to check the deployments and pods using kubectl. \n\nSo, the tool call would be exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd with the command "kubectl get deployments -n astronomy-shop" to check the deployments. \n\nAlternatively, "kubectl get pods -n astronomy-shop" to check the pods. \n\nBut the user might need to check both. However, since the user can only make one tool call, they need to choose one. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the user should check the metrics for each service. \n\nBut again, without knowing the exact metric names, it\'s hard. \n\nAlternatively, the user could use get_operations for one of the services to find out the operations, which can then be used in the metrics queries. \n\nFor example, using get_operations on the cart service. \n\nSo, the next tool call would be get_operations with service "cart". \n\nBut the user hasn\'t done that yet. \n\nHmm. The user\'s previous steps were to get services and the dependency graph. Now, the next step is to check the health of the services. \n\nSo, the best next step is to check the deployments and pods using kubectl. \n\nTherefore, the tool call would be exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd with the command "kubectl get deployments -n astronomy-shop". \n\nBut the user might need to check the pods as well. \n\nAlternatively, the user could check the pods first. \n\nBut given the available tools, the user should proceed with checking the deployments and pods. \n\nSo, the next tool call is exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd with the command "kubectl get deployments -n astronomy-shop".\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get deployments -n astronomy-shop"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-af21d016b9b7d0be', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 1858, 'prompt_tokens': 2679, 'total_tokens': 4537, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbd9-c60b-7633-9096-69949fdd50d5-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get deployments -n astronomy-shop'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-af21d016b9b7d0be', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2679, 'output_tokens': 1858, 'total_tokens': 4537}), ToolMessage(content='NAME              READY   UP-TO-DATE   AVAILABLE   AGE\naccounting        1/1     1            1           2m48s\nad                1/1     1            1           2m48s\ncart              1/1     1            1           2m48s\ncheckout          1/1     1            1           2m48s\ncurrency          1/1     1            1           2m48s\nemail             1/1     1            1           2m48s\nflagd             1/1     1            1           2m48s\nfraud-detection   1/1     1            1           2m48s\nfrontend          0/2     2            0           54s\nfrontend-proxy    1/1     1            1           2m48s\ngrafana           1/1     1            1           2m48s\nimage-provider    1/1     1            1           2m48s\njaeger            1/1     1            1           2m48s\nkafka             1/1     1            1           2m48s\nllm               1/1     1            1           2m48s\nload-generator    1/1     1            1           2m48s\npayment           1/1     1            1       