er tool calls weren\'t necessary. \n\nSo, the final answer should focus on the missing readiness probe in product-catalog as the main issue, leading to the frontend\'s inability to connect properly.\n</think>\n\nsubmit_tool  \n{"ans": "The root cause of the frontend readiness issues is the absence of a readiness probe in the `product-catalog` deployment. This causes Kubernetes to incorrectly mark the pod as \'Ready\' without verifying the application is operational, leading to connection failures and timeouts. The `ad` and `cart` services may also have similar misconfigurations, but `product-catalog` is the most direct culprit."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 482, 'prompt_tokens': 18284, 'total_tokens': 18766, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbdd-e8a3-7d90-96f8-c9a9da152b79-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 18284, 'output_tokens': 482, 'total_tokens': 18766}), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='6b87542e-5808-46e2-aa7f-2ad443851486'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is trying to diagnose an issue with the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application. The main problem seems to be with the frontend service not being ready, and they\'ve been using various tools to check the status of pods, deployments, metrics, and traces.\n\nFirst, they used `get_services` to list all the services in the namespace, which gave them a list including `cart`, `flagd`, `frontend-proxy`, and others. Then, they checked the deployments and pods to see the current state. The frontend had 