ool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 17518, 'output_tokens': 491, 'total_tokens': 18009}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='32db3a5f-adc6-4fb1-8ff4-5c341c9f9a3f'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is trying to diagnose an issue with the frontend service in their OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application. They\'ve been using various tools to check the status of pods, deployments, metrics, and traces.\n\nFirst, they used `get_services` to list the services in Grafana, which gave them a list including `cart`, `flagd`, and `frontend-proxy`. Then, they checked the deployments and pods to see the current state. The frontend pods were showing as not ready, which is a problem.\n\nThey ran `get_metrics` to check the readiness of the frontend pods and found that some were not ready. Then they looked into the traces for the frontend service to see if there were any errors or failures in the calls to dependent services. The traces showed some successful calls but also some issues, like a PostgreSQL query that might have been a problem.\n\nNext, they checked the readiness probes for the `product-catalog`, `ad`, and `cart` services. The `product-catalog` deployment didn\'t have a readiness probe configured, which means Kubernetes wasn\'t checking if the service was actually ready before routing traffic to it. This could cause the frontend to fail when trying to connect to `product-catalog`.\n\nThe user then tried to confirm this by getting the deployment YAML for `product-catalog` and confirmed that there was no `readinessProbe` section. This solidified the conclusion that the missing readiness probe was the root cause. The `ad` service\'s deployment didn\'t show any issues, so the main problem was with `product-catalog`.\n\nSo, the final answer points to the absence of a readiness probe in the `product-catalog` deployment as the root cause. This causes the frontend to fail connecting to the service, leading to readiness issues. The user then submitted this as the answer using the `submit_tool` function.\n</think>\n\nsubmit_tool  \n{"ans": "The root cause of the frontend readiness issues is the absence of a readiness probe in the `product-catalog` deployment. This causes Kubernetes to incorrectly mark the pod as \'Ready\' without verifying the application is operational, leading to connection failures and timeouts. The `ad` and `cart` services may also have similar misconfigurations, but `product-catalog` is the most direct culprit."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 481, 'prompt_tokens': 18510, 'total_tokens': 18991, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbde-1be1-7522-a64a-63b096ae319e-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 18510, 'output_tokens': 481, 'total_tokens': 18991}), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='bf6ea37c-57d9-4eae-a52a-d9a85f9eda08'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is trying to diagnose an issue with the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application. The main problem seems to be with the frontend service not being ready, and they\'ve been using various tools to check the status of pods, deployments, metrics, and traces.\n\nFirst, they used `get_services` to list all the services in the namespace, which gave them a list including `cart`, `flagd`, and `frontend-proxy`. Then, they checked the deployments and pods to see the current state. The frontend deployment had